  "annotation": {
    "schema_version": 5,
    "type": "new architecture support",
    "problem": [
      {
        "text": "CohereForCausalLM needs an architecture registration and a constructor mapping its checkpoint tensors to shared modules.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_007e13b535714f2291fa9b3baa9df907",
          "call_cae5db434bca4573862b9b0a35311bb6"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "reasoning": [
      {
        "text": "The implementation combines shared-input parallel decoder blocks, LayerNorm, GPTJ-style RoPE and output-logit scaling rather than introducing new attention kernels. Reusing these components reduces architecture-specific execution code, but also inherits their limits.",
        "basis": "inference",
        "evidence": [
          "call_cae5db434bca4573862b9b0a35311bb6",
          "call_8ce7bc11687a4297a3436ef7977a5158",
          "call_0efe00ff77a94998a14817dc08d9a68d"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "impact": [
      {
        "text": "Config.from_directory can now select CohereConfig, whose model_class is CohereModel. Registration does not establish compatibility with every checkpoint declaring CohereForCausalLM: Command R+ requires Q/K normalization absent from the selected Attention implementation.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_007e13b535714f2291fa9b3baa9df907",
          "call_975ac99230d5424d816387cd6e6dd32f",
          "call_cae5db434bca4573862b9b0a35311bb6",
          "call_49a4d09a1fb44909afa10d2b7c054eec",
          "call_0efe00ff77a94998a14817dc08d9a68d"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "source_notes": [
      {
        "text": "The parallel-decoder ancestor records shared-normalization composition and conditional failures for missing components or plain MLP allocation. The output-scale ancestor establishes the previously unused post_scale mechanism. The original models chapter describes the common architecture factory and checkpoint-mapping pattern.",
        "basis": "ancestor",
        "evidence": [
          "call_44e5a1165ac3406bb0841cbf67a34c70",
          "call_161ade8503b04a8cb4e084d52906e2b1",
          "call_5d33466ef3be438ab7bbaa2d99ef794f"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Those parallel-block inconsistencies remain in the unchanged implementation, but Cohere supplies all three components and uses GatedMLP, avoiding the recorded triggers.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_cae5db434bca4573862b9b0a35311bb6",
          "call_8ce7bc11687a4297a3436ef7977a5158"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Parent-tree Cohere occurrences include the architecture roadmap and an existing chat template; architecture execution support is distinct from prompt formatting.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_dcf3470ba45a45099e85fcc8a1f62456",
          "call_007e13b535714f2291fa9b3baa9df907"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The inspected discussions are \u201cquantizing model: undefined symbol: __cxa_call_terminate,\u201d \u201c`cogito-v1-preview-qwen-32B` generates incoherent output for bpw <= 2.5,\u201d and \u201cBuild Failure on Windows: CUDA 12.4 / PyTorch 2.7.0+cu126 / VS 2022.\u201d They concern extension loading, quantization quality and compilation, respectively; none identifies this Cohere addition as its remedy.",
        "basis": "source",
