    "chapters": [
      {
        "id": "models",
        "title": "Cohere architecture assembly and checkpoint compatibility",
        "claims": [
          {
            "text": "Dispatch remains based on the single architectures entry in config.json. The new registry entry selects CohereConfig; Model.from_config then constructs its CohereModel. The registration and constructor are complementary: the former exposes the latter through the normal factory.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_007e13b535714f2291fa9b3baa9df907",
              "call_975ac99230d5424d816387cd6e6dd32f",
              "call_98b8d0c4a9054fe2bd7b82704a139e6c",
              "call_cae5db434bca4573862b9b0a35311bb6"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "CohereConfig reads residual width, MLP width, layer count and query/KV head counts. Missing KV count defaults to query count; missing or zero head_dim becomes hidden_size // num_attention_heads. It permits absent hidden_act but rejects a supplied value other than silu. LayerNorm epsilon defaults to 1e-5, tied embeddings to true, and logit_scale to 0.0625. Shared RoPE configuration reads theta, scaling and position limits, with GPTJ style supplied by Cohere.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_cae5db434bca4573862b9b0a35311bb6",
              "call_975ac99230d5424d816387cd6e6dd32f"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Each block computes y = LayerNorm(x), then x += Attention(y) and x += GatedMLP(y). Both branches consume the same normalized input; \u201cparallel\u201d denotes their dependency structure, not concurrent scheduling. The normalizer requests half output. The final model.norm also produces half output before lm_head.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_cae5db434bca4573862b9b0a35311bb6",
              "call_8ce7bc11687a4297a3436ef7977a5158",
              "call_364985f6716f4e6a9153f30b3ca279a1"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Checkpoint names are model.embed_tokens, model.layers.i.input_layernorm, self_attn.{q,k,v,o}_proj, mlp.{up,gate,down}_proj, model.norm and lm_head. For residual width H, intermediate width I and head width D, Attention constructs Q [QD,H], K/V [KD,H] and O [H,QD] projections. The head offers model.embed_tokens as an alternate key when tying is enabled and the constructor's lm_head check fails; Linear still tries its primary key before the alternate within each supported storage path.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_cae5db434bca4573862b9b0a35311bb6",
              "call_0efe00ff77a94998a14817dc08d9a68d",
              "call_9340ae05aaa04911848d120a0f6fc7ad"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "logit_scale is passed to Linear.post_scale, which multiplies the backend output in place after optional softcapping. Cohere supplies no softcap, so its head applies a direct output multiplier, not a weight-storage transformation. head_bits remains the separate head quantization budget.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_cae5db434bca4573862b9b0a35311bb6",
              "call_9340ae05aaa04911848d120a0f6fc7ad"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "prepare_inputs follows the inspected Llama, Phi3, Gemma, GLM4 and DeciLM call sites: retain input_ids in params, then call prepare_for_attn without additional guards. The helper defaults to uncached FlashAttention, rejects caches for uncached modes, and checks batch-shaped cached requests. Model.prefill sets prefill only at the last KV-affecting block; ParallelDecoderBlock then returns after attention's residual addition and skips its MLP.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_b4e23dbb214c4e0992a4e56dd2ee44e6",
              "call_74f8eee9778b4b26aa03e0c294360f18",
              "call_0efe00ff77a94998a14817dc08d9a68d",
              "call_98b8d0c4a9054fe2bd7b82704a139e6c",
              "call_8ce7bc11687a4297a3436ef7977a5158"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "CohereLabs/aya-23-8B supplies H=4096, I=14336, 32 layers and Q/K=32/8; aya-23-35B supplies H=8192, I=22528, 40 layers and Q/K=64/64. Both use epsilon 1e-5, scale 0.0625 and use_qk_norm=false. Their sampled projection and MLP headers agree with the constructor dimensions; the 8B embedding is [256000,4096].",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_94593f009e8e4abba94ef77c5b3e6199",
              "call_2db3d65ff7724a86b3c4f06c3b0330f4",
              "call_183f88967cab4ab18ce99f7195b3d250",
              "call_dfd7350a32c24d4b9224d5bb86b8aae4"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "CohereLabs/aya-expanse-8b retains the 4096/14336, 32-layer, 32/8-head dimensions but explicitly changes scale to 0.125, which overrides the default. aya-expanse-32b uses H=8192, I=24576, 40 layers and 64/8 heads with scale 0.0625. Both disable Q/K normalization. Sampled headers match their respective dimensions, including K/V width 1024.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_08a2f72cecae4df3978f3f0b82071986",
              "call_dac6c9f8c1ac41fb834cc076f00e8d25",
              "call_f1f544a25d0140daac0615cc70e432ca",
              "call_5bf2bf7e2d754bf089c0a3d0b7bf921d"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "CohereLabs/c4ai-command-r-v01 uses the 8192/22528, 40-layer, 64/64-head layout, explicitly ties embeddings and specifies scale 0.0625. Its sampled embedding and square attention matrices match. c4ai-command-r-08-2024 instead uses I=24576 and eight KV heads, matching its sampled [1024,8192] K/V matrices; its config disables Q/K normalization and retains scale 0.0625.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_9651902e135f4363842d9a130fedfb13",
              "call_1fd566b0c4c8413ab3dfd6e6dbed7607",
              "call_34b2d9df655d490cac7379d0851b541c",
              "call_52a4d44ddcdb4c8c817f6617b8712b1e"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "CohereLabs/c4ai-command-r-plus and c4ai-command-r-plus-08-2024 both use H=12288, I=33792, 64 layers, 96/8 heads and scale 0.8333333333333334. Their sampled linear matrices match those dimensions, but both enable use_qk_norm and store q_norm.weight [96,128] and k_norm.weight [8,128]. The new constructor and shared Attention never load or apply those tensors.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_49a4d09a1fb44909afa10d2b7c054eec",
              "call_a1082472c24a4a42b4c96f01c41dc645",
              "call_19da404c81d643aba855b6c3aa58f41f",
              "call_11ba769cf989423b9e4c078d7e5cb647",
              "call_cae5db434bca4573862b9b0a35311bb6",
              "call_0efe00ff77a94998a14817dc08d9a68d"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "CohereLabs/c4ai-command-r-v01-4bit and c4ai-command-r-plus-4bit retain their corresponding base dimensions and scales but declare bitsandbytes FP4 storage. Sampled MLP weights are U8 [92274688,1] and [207618048,1], not dense [I,H] matrices. Their absmax, quant_map and quant_state.bitsandbytes__fp4 tensors have no reader in the inspected Linear loading paths, which implement EXL3 or ordinary weights rather than bitsandbytes decoding.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_380772f5bc6444858e175ab6f7ec96db",
              "call_53c26225f97f439084742913bf76354a",
              "call_59a083dbeea44ab58ba52d3c24dd35c4",
              "call_ddb7732d382e445b89e9702c52755e85",
              "call_9340ae05aaa04911848d120a0f6fc7ad"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "A scalar metadata check derived head_dim=128 for all four distinct dimension families and verified that their linear widths, including vocabulary size 256000, are multiples of Linear's 128-element padding unit. It also evaluated the configured scales as 1/16, 1/8 and 5/6 and reproduced the two packed MLP element counts as H\u00d7I/2.",
            "basis": "execution",
            "evidence": [
              "call_bfeaa3de8504466abb2555975c9a6efa",
              "call_9340ae05aaa04911848d120a0f6fc7ad"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "findings": [
      {
        "id": "cohere-qk-normalization-omitted",
        "origin": "authoring_observation",
        "status": "suspected",
        "classification": "defect",
        "description": "Architecture registration includes Command R+ configurations requiring Q/K normalization, but the constructed attention path omits it.",
        "trigger": "Construct and run a CohereForCausalLM checkpoint with use_qk_norm=true, such as either inspected dense Command R+ release.",
        "expected_behavior": "Apply the checkpoint's Q/K normalization or explicitly reject that unsupported configuration.",
        "actual_behavior": "CohereConfig does not read or reject use_qk_norm. Attention projects and reshapes Q/K, then applies RoPE; all three attention implementations retain TODO comments for Q/K norms. Stored q_norm and k_norm weights are unused.",
